From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:50:40 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the SHA-3 instructions

EOR3, BCAX, RAX1 and XAR (FEAT_SHA3) are added as intrinsics, under
their assembly names like the SHA-2 ones. They compute the column
parities, the theta and rho rotations and the chi step of
Keccak-f[1600], with two 64-bit state words per register: EOR3 and
BCAX work on the whole register, RAX1 and XAR on its two 64-bit
elements. XAR rotates the XOR of its operands right by an immediate
from 0 to 63, checked at assembly generation. So the rho rotation by r
is XAR by 64 - r, as a lemma in armv8a_simd_lemmas.v states, or XAR by
0 when r is 0.

The semantics follow DDI 0487 M.d, C7.2, and all four are
data-independent-time instructions (C5.2.4). FEAT_SHA3 is optional,
and the compiler doesn't check that the target implements it (#505).

Co-authored-by: orvenweb3 <orvenweb3@gmail.com>
